## Inventory

Inspect and understand these files.

### 1) Configuration entrypoints and workspace wiring

| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `./.bazelrc` | The main Bazel configuration file defining common build options, spawn strategies, and specific configuration flag sets for different hardware backends (CPU, GPU, XPU). It includes directives to import configuration generated by scripts and user-specific files. |
| `./.bazelrc.user` | Contains user-specific or environment-specific Bazel build overrides. It typically holds host-specific compiler paths (like `icpx`), compiler and linker flags, and oneAPI-related environment variables used during the build process. |
| `./.itex_configure.bazelrc` | Generated automatically by the `./configure.py` script. It explicitly stores host-local environment variables and configurations, such as Python binary/library paths, TensorFlow headers/shared libraries locations, and SYCL/oneAPI toolkit paths. These host-local paths are intentional for the build environment. |
| `./WORKSPACE` | The root Bazel workspace file. It defines the workspace name, verifies Bazel versions, loads Python and TensorFlow configurations, sets up Intel Extension for OpenXLA repositories, and calls the primary ITEX workspace initialization macros (`itex_workspace1()` and `itex_workspace()`). |
| `./itex/workspace.bzl` | Defines the core `itex_workspace` macro. It is responsible for fetching and pinning the majority of core external dependencies for ITEX. Notably, it handles oneDNN version pinning and sets up crucial repositories like `onednn_cpu`, `onednn_gpu`, `onednn_cpu_eigen`, `sycl_configure`, `pybind11`, and `absl`. |
| `./itex/workspace1.bzl` | Defines the initial `workspace` setup macro (aliased as `itex_workspace1` in `WORKSPACE`). It loads foundational tooling and compiler dependencies early in the build sequence, such as `bazel_skylib`, `rules_pkg`, and the raw `llvm-project` repositories. |
| `./itex/tf_configure.bzl` | Contains the `tf_configure` repository rule logic. It sets up TensorFlow as an external dependency by dynamically querying the local Python environment for TensorFlow C++ headers, shared libraries, and ABI flags required to successfully compile ITEX against the installed TensorFlow wheel. |

### 2) Core entrypoints / backend

- Read:
| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `./itex/itex.bzl` | Defines core Bazel build configurations, macros, and compiler options (e.g., `tf_copts`, backend selectors) used throughout the ITEX project. |
| `./itex/BUILD` | The main Bazel BUILD file for the ITEX project. Defines configuration settings for different backends (CPU AVX2/AVX512, GPU) and builds the primary shared libraries. |
| `./itex/core/kernels/BUILD` | Bazel BUILD file for the ITEX XPU kernel library. Packages core kernel implementations and wires CPU/GPU specific kernel dependencies. |
| `./itex/core/graph/BUILD` | Bazel BUILD file for ITEX graph optimization. Defines libraries for the `xpu_optimizer`, integrating passes like layout and mixed precision optimization. |
| `./itex/core/devices/BUILD` | Bazel BUILD file for device utilities and memory allocators. Defines targets like `xpu_device` and `bfc_allocator` to abstract hardware management. |
| `./itex/core/devices/gpu/BUILD` | Bazel BUILD file for GPU runtime components. Builds libraries for GPU device plugins, Eigen stream devices, and the underlying SYCL runtime. |
| `./itex/core/utils/onednn/onednn_util.h` | Central adapter between ITEX kernels and oneDNN. |
| `./itex/core/devices/next_pluggable_device/gpu_device_plugin.cc` | Implements the C API for TensorFlow's Next Pluggable Device architecture, registering the "XPU" device and routing buffer/shape conversions. |
| `./itex/core/wrapper/itex_gpu_wrapper.cc` | Dynamic library wrapper for the GPU backend. Handles early initialization (`LoadGpuLibrary`), configures XLA flags, and provides mock functions for the plugin API. |
| `./itex/core/wrapper/itex_cpu_wrapper.cc` | Dynamic library wrapper for the CPU backend. Dynamically loads the optimized CPU backend library (AVX512 or AVX2) and oneDNN based on hardware capabilities. |
| `./itex/tools/pip_package/BUILD` | Defines Bazel rules and dependencies for building the `intel_extension_for_tensorflow` pip package, gathering required shared libraries and Python headers. |
| `./itex/core/utils/BUILD` | Bazel BUILD file for core ITEX utilities. Compiles foundational components like logging, string manipulation, and environment variable parsing. |
| `./itex/core/utils/build_config.bzl` | Provides platform-specific build configurations and Bazel macros (like `tf_deps`, `pyx_library`, `cc_proto`) for managing external dependencies and extensions. |
| `./itex/python/build_defs.bzl` | Defines custom Bazel macros (`pybind_extension`, `pybind_library`) for building Python extensions using Pybind11 with correct linking and rpaths. |
| `./third_party/repo.bzl` | Bazel utility macros for fetching and managing external repositories, including `tf_http_archive` for handling downloads and patching dependencies. |
| `./itex/core/graph/xpu_graph.cc` | Highest-signal runtime graph wiring entrypoint. Registers the ITEX Grappler optimizer, selects CPU vs XPU device type, disables conflicting TensorFlow passes, initializes env-driven graph settings, and emits debug wiring logs. |
| `./itex/core/graph/xpu_optimizer.cc` | Entrypoint for the XPU Graph Optimizer. Implements creation and execution of graph optimization passes via TensorFlow's Grappler API. |
| `./itex/core/graph/xpu_optimizer.h` | Runtime callback contract for Grappler registration. Declares the create/optimize/destroy hooks and device-scoped optimizer object that `xpu_graph.cc` binds into TensorFlow. |
| `./itex/core/kernels/xpu_kernel.cc` | Core registry initialization for ITEX kernels. Handles the dispatch logic to register CPU or GPU kernels depending on the active backend. |
| `./itex/core/devices/xpu_device_util.h` | Low-level device utility bridge showing how templated fill/memset/memcpy operations dispatch to either Eigen threadpool code or the ITEX GPU stream runtime under backend-specific compile guards. |
| `./itex/core/graph/xpu_graph.h` | Thin ABI boundary for graph-plugin initialization. Exposes `TF_InitGraph_Internal`, which is the TensorFlow-facing hook used to register ITEX graph optimizers. |
| `./itex/core/graph/optimizer_config.cc` | Implementation logic for retrieving ITEX optimizer configuration flags from environment variables or protobufs, falling back to legacy variable names. |
| `./itex/core/devices/xpu_device.cc` | Implementation of standard device lifecycle operations (create, destroy). Routes generic device API calls to the corresponding CPU or GPU backend. |
| `./itex/core/kernels/onednn_graph/onednn_graph_op.cc` | Integration for executing operations via oneDNN Graph. Defines engine creation and memory allocation wrappers (`sycl_malloc_wrapper`) for the graph compiler. |
| `./itex/core/devices/gpu/itex_gpu_runtime.cc` | Provides the SYCL-based GPU runtime for ITEX. Manages device pools, contexts, and abstractions for interacting with underlying Intel GPU hardware via Level-Zero. |

### 3) SYCL enablement and crosstool wiring

| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `./third_party/build_option/BUILD` | A minimal BUILD file setting default public visibility, marking the `build_option` directory as a Bazel package. |
| `./third_party/build_option/sycl_configure.bzl` | Starlark repository rule (`sycl_configure`) that autoconfigures the SYCL toolchain. It inspects environment variables (e.g., `HOST_CXX_COMPILER`, `SYCL_TOOLKIT_PATH`) to locate host and SYCL compilers and populate repository templates. |
| `./third_party/build_option/crosstool_sycl/BUILD` | A minimal BUILD file setting default public visibility for the `crosstool_sycl` package. |
| `./third_party/build_option/crosstool_sycl/BUILD.tpl` | A template for the `BUILD` file of the auto-generated SYCL crosstool repository. It defines the `cc_toolchain` and `cc_toolchain_suite` for `toolchain-linux-x86_64` utilizing the custom SYCL compiler wrapper. |
| `./third_party/build_option/crosstool_sycl/cc_toolchain_config.bzl.tpl` | A template for the `cc_toolchain_config` Starlark rule. It configures the SYCL C++ toolchains on Linux, defining action configurations, compilation flags, and linking behaviors. |
| `./third_party/build_option/crosstool_sycl/bin/BUILD` | A minimal BUILD file setting default public visibility for the `bin` subdirectory of the crosstool package. |
| `./third_party/build_option/crosstool_sycl/bin/crosstool_wrapper_driver.tpl` | A Python script template acting as a compiler wrapper. It intercepts compilation actions, forwarding device-side code to the SYCL compiler (like `icpx`) with appropriate SYCL flags (e.g., `-fsycl`) and delegating host code compilation. |
| `./third_party/build_option/sycl/BUILD` | Defines `cc_library` targets (`itex_gpu_header`, `eigen_itex_gpu_header`) and the `build_with_sycl` configuration setting for local SYCL packages. |
| `./third_party/build_option/sycl/BUILD.tpl` | A template for the `local_config_sycl` external repository BUILD file. It exposes the `itex_gpu_headers` library and declares config settings for SYCL, XeTLA, and NextPluggableDevice integrations. |
| `./third_party/build_option/sycl/platform.bzl.tpl` | A Starlark template containing basic utility functions, such as `sycl_library_path`, to handle SYCL platform-specific operations. |
| `./third_party/build_option/sycl/build_defs.bzl.tpl` | A Starlark template defining macros (e.g., `if_sycl`, `if_xetla`, `if_sycl_build_is_configured`) used to conditionally add dependencies or compile flags based on whether SYCL or XeTLA was enabled during configuration. |

### 4) oneDNN Bazel integration and link topology

| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `./third_party/onednn/onednn.bzl` | Contains Starlark utility functions (`convert_cl_to_cpp`, `convert_header_to_cpp`, `gen_onednn_version`) used within genrules to dynamically generate oneDNN C++ source files and headers from templates or OpenCL files. |
| `./third_party/onednn/build_defs.bzl` | Defines `select()` macros (e.g., `onednn_deps`, `onednn_graph_deps`, `if_cpu_onednn`) that pull in the correct set of oneDNN library dependencies depending on whether ITEX is being built for CPU or GPU. |
| `./third_party/onednn/onednn_cpu.BUILD` | The primary Bazel BUILD file for building the oneDNN CPU library from source. It configures CMake define templates (`dnnl_config_h`) specifying Threadpool/THREADPOOL/OMP thread runtimes and CPU ISA optimizations (AVX2, AVX512, etc.). |
| `./third_party/onednn/onednn_gpu.BUILD` | The Bazel BUILD file for building the oneDNN GPU library from source. It configures CMake definitions specific to SYCL, DPCPP, Level Zero, and enables Intel GPU vendor backends. |
| `./third_party/onednn/onednn_cpu_eigen.BUILD` | A Bazel BUILD file tailored for compiling oneDNN for CPU integrated with Eigen. It shares a nearly identical structure to `onednn_cpu.BUILD`, configuring the thread execution runtimes and graph dependencies. |

